# p5 mcp: what the model is told when a server refuses a call with a JSON-RPC
# error. The run's loopback HTTP MCP server (`mcphttp`) is ready at launch;
# turn one calls its tool by name and it answers; then it refuses every
# request (`rpcerror`, -32603 `fixture refuses`) and turn two calls it again.
# fx v0.0.16 tells the model `MCP protocol error -32603: fixture refuses`
# (`write_protocol_diagnostic`, src/core/mcp/tool_result.zig:199-214@481104fd).
mcphttp ready
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-live-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-live-profile.json
gateway p5-mcp-rpcerror-turns.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=full-access
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
wait 6
type use the web echo tool
key Enter
wait 6
mcphttp rpcerror
type and once more
key Enter
wait 6
snap failed
gwlog
